Fault models, prospective current and time scale (@pe-faults: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @electrical-power-engineering, #source "../sources/Sistemas-Eletricos-de-Potencia-Bichels.lingua#r_5T4SVBJ6FAPQWJPVNQV4Y6427G", #source "../sources/Power-System-Protection-Soman-NPTEL.lingua#r_52Z22QR7WGDJHAFBDMPFGYCXJE", #source "../sources/Electrical-Standards-Edition-and-Jurisdiction.lingua#r_169QEF26N0C345MKSRWQY6KD90", #electrical-power-engineering "../../../physics/electromagnetism/induction/Quasistatic-limits-diffusion-and-skin-depth.lingua#r_7RSC1KG4B4DNB7C7319F691MSW") { r_4FV98NRVV0M3JYR5WG3X2E8KVS
**Read:** [Sistemas elétricos de potência — Arlei Bichels](../sources/Sistemas-Eletricos-de-Potencia-Bichels.lingua#r_5T4SVBJ6FAPQWJPVNQV4Y6427G), complete fault and component models; [Power System Protection — S. A. Soman, IIT Bombay](../sources/Power-System-Protection-Soman-NPTEL.lingua#r_52Z22QR7WGDJHAFBDMPFGYCXJE), all sequence/fault and apparatus lectures; [Electrical standards, edition and jurisdiction](../sources/Electrical-Standards-Edition-and-Jurisdiction.lingua#r_169QEF26N0C345MKSRWQY6KD90), complete applicable short-circuit method, edition and scope.

A fault calculation predicts current/voltage under a specified abnormal connection, source state and time scale. Define fault type/location/impedance, prefault operating state, network topology and source models. A bolted three-phase fault is one ideal case; actual arcing, earth and intermittent faults can behave differently.

For a simple positive-sequence Thévenin model, initial symmetrical fault current is determined by prefault source voltage divided by the stated source/network/fault impedance. Generator subtransient, transient and steady behavior differ, and converter limits cannot automatically be represented by the same source reactance. Include motors or other connected sources where they contribute.

Compare maximum and minimum credible fault currents for different source/topology/operating conditions. Equipment interruption/withstand and relay sensitivity impose different questions; the largest current is not the only important case. Check units, per-unit bases, phase connections, earth/neutral return paths and current-transformer measurements. A steady fault equivalent does not reproduce DC offset, current-zero timing or a travelling surge, which the next transient and apparatus Records address separately.

